# Copy to config/dsh.env (gitignored), fill explicit API settings; never commit keys.
# Use an existing DSH 0.2.1-rc.5 executable. Bootstrap never installs or mutates it.
# DANUS_DSH_BIN=/absolute/path/to/dsh
# DANUS_DSH_PROVIDER=danus-api
# DANUS_DSH_API=openai-responses
# DANUS_DSH_API_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway.example/v1
# DANUS_DSH_API_KEY=your-key
# DANUS_MAIN_MODEL=your-model
# DANUS_MAIN_EFFORT=high
# DANUS_DSH_REASONING_EFFORTS=high,xhigh  # only gateway-supported identity mappings
# scripts/setup-dsh.sh writes a credential-free JSON provider overlay here:
# DANUS_DSH_PROVIDER_PATCH=/absolute/path/runtime/dsh-provider.json
# For custom model metadata/effort mappings provide your own JSON patch instead
# of running setup-dsh.sh. All route fields and model/effort support are explicit.

# Optional worker-only project route; set BOTH or fail closed. Keys still live
# here, referenced by apiKeyEnv in that provider patch. No legacy API_* fallback.
# DANUS_PROJECT_MYPROJECT_WORKER_DSH_PROVIDER=project-api
# DANUS_PROJECT_MYPROJECT_WORKER_DSH_PROVIDER_PATCH=/absolute/path/project-provider.json
# MYPROJECT_API_KEY=your-project-key
